      "writtenOn": "2026-01-15T21:32:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So what is being passed around here isn\u0027t really a \"simulations\" but a \"here is a bunch of information on how to re-create the font I wanted\". CoreText has a similar idea with [flattening the attributes](https://developer.apple.com/library/archive/documentation/StringsTextFonts/Conceptual/CoreText_Programming/FontOperations/FontOperations.html#//apple_ref/doc/uid/TP40005533-CH4-SW25). In general this would want to be a type with a typeface factory id (or some id so the format of the data is known) and an sk_sp\u003cSkData\u003e.\n\nIf this where all Chromium side I would say land this all and we\u0027ll fix it up later. However, this being on the Skia side I\u0027d like to make sure we get this at least somewhat logically correct first.",
      "revId": "a18594fdb4576bb0579d22827878471452d62367",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0c12e69e_56218df9",
        "filename": "include/core/SkFontArguments.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-15T21:57:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Note to self: such extended attributes should also be passed through SkFontDescriptor and get serialized and deserialized (with the \"typeface factory tag\" or \"extra format tag\" so that the typeface factories can decide if they can apply the data).\n\nAlso, this is related to the issues around being able to deserialize typeface data properly on the receiving end. Like with the CoreText hvgl format issues (where CoreText will create them as system fonts but not from data) where it becomes necessary to serialize into a different format. In this case the issue is the the format is \"mostly standard\" but with \"extra implementation bits\" on the side.",
      "parentUuid": "b297d501_fc16631e",
      "revId": "a18594fdb4576bb0579d22827878471452d62367",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "149fae3e_e44e2207",
        "filename": "include/core/SkFontArguments.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 3726077
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-16T17:17:31Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Makes sense, and +1 to doing it right the first time.\n\nI changed the \"simulations flags\" everywhere to instead be a struct that contains the typeface factory ID and an opaque `SkData` blob. The corresponding typeface can create/deserialize it as needed, and it should be extensible if required.\n\nPTAL and let me know if that addresses your concerns!",
      "parentUuid": "0c12e69e_56218df9",
      "revId": "a18594fdb4576bb0579d22827878471452d62367",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "22968d8c_2eb56b2a",
        "filename": "include/core/SkFontArguments.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 100,
      "author": {
        "id": 5140
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-01-23T22:15:38Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So for CoreText we would need an opaque bit of data for sure, but after a lot of thinking it seems synthetic bold and oblique should probably be called out directly since in theory FontConfig typefaces can specify synthetic bold and it is possible that other backends could also offer such synthetics. The other existing parameters aren\u0027t really that different, one can specify a bunch of variation axis locations for font data that doesn\u0027t have any axes or even to a backend that doesn\u0027t support them at all.\n\nAlso, we do want this to get plumbed through serialization. And cloning. And some testing. So I went and did https://skia-review.googlesource.com/c/skia/+/1148216 .",
      "parentUuid": "149fae3e_e44e2207",
      "revId": "a18594fdb4576bb0579d22827878471452d62367",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
